    <section id="reflections">
      <h2>My Academic Journey</h2>
      <p>
        Currently, I am in my first year of study at Botswana School of Business Sciences (BAC), pursuing a degree in Network Systems Engineering.
        I have been learning about various aspects of networking, including network protocols, security, and system administration.
        Through the use of CISCO tools such as Packet Tracer, I have also been working on projects that involve designing and implementing network solutions, which has helped me develop practical skills in the field.
        I have also been learning about programming languages such as HTML and JavaScript, which has allowed me to create web applications and gain a better understanding of how networks and systems interact with one another.
        Part of my academic journey has also involved working on group projects, which has helped me develop teamwork and communication skills, as well as the ability to work effectively in a collaborative environment.
        At the end of my first year, I will have gained a solid foundation in networking and systems engineering, which will prepare me for more advanced coursework and practical experience in the field.
        My academic journey has been challenging, but also rewarding, and I am excited to continue learning and growing as a network systems engineer.
        These micro-projects have given me a better understanding of how HTML and JavaScript work.
        I also learned how to use GitHub to manage and share my code with others, which has been a valuable skill in the field of software development.
        The micro-projects have also helped me develop problem-solving skills, as I have had to troubleshoot issues and find solutions to challenges that arise during the development process.
        One of the biggest adjustments for me was managing a busier timeble. 
        At first I found this difficult because I am used to a flexible timetable which allowed me some spare time but now, in tertiary level, I have realised that I have to manage my time well so that I am able to achieve my non-academic goals. 
      </p>

      <h2>Group Work Reflection</h2>
      <p>
        My group began with the forming stage, where we got to know each other and established our goals and objectives for the project.</p>

        <p>During the storming stage we encountered some challenges and conflicts, but we were able to work through the issues and establish a more effective way of working together. 
        One of the challenges we faced was communication, as we had different ideas and opinions about how to approach the project. 
        However, we were able to overcome this by actively listening to each other and finding common ground.</p>

        <p>In the norming stage, we established clear roles and responsibilities, and developed a sense of trust and respect for each other. 
        We also established a more structured approach to our work, which helped us to be more efficient and affective in our collaboration.</p>

        <p>In the performing stage, we were able to work together effectively and achieve our goals. 
        We were able to leverage each other's strengths and skills to produce high-quality work and deliver a successful project. 
        We also learned to communicate more effectively and provide constructive feedback to each other, which helped us to improve our work and achieve better results.</p>

        <p>Finally, in the adjourning stage we reflected on our experience and celebrated our successes. 
        We also discussed areas for improvement and identified ways to apply what we learned to future projects. 
        Overall, our group experience was a valuable learning opportnity that helped us to develop important skills such as communication, collaboration, and problem-solving, which will be useful in our future careers.</p>
      
    </section>

